<BaseLayout title="Interrupts" description="SIGRUN interrupt plumbing: the GDT and TSS, a 256-entry IDT with exception handlers, and the APIC/PIC controllers that route device interrupts.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Subsystem 5 · interrupts</p>
  <h1>Interrupts: GDT, IDT, exceptions, and the APIC</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Interrupts are how hardware talks to the kernel. SIGRUN builds the three tables the CPU consults — GDT,
    IDT, TSS — installs handlers for every exception, and routes device interrupts through the Local APIC
    instead of the legacy PIC.
  </p>

